3. This Keyword and Static Members
➢ Static Members
    Belong to the class itself, not to any specific object.
    Declared using the static keyword.
    Accessed via the class name: ClassName.StaticMember.

   public class Student
   {
       public static float gpa_S = 8;
   }
   class Program
   {
       Student s = new Student();
       Console.Write(Student.gpa_S);
   }                                                           35

3. This Keyword and Static Members
➢ Static Methods
    Static methods can only access static members. They
     cannot directly access non-static instance members.

     public class Student
     {   string _id, _name; float _gpa;
         static float gpa_S = 8;
         public static bool Scholarship()
         {
             if (_gpa >= gpa_S)
                return 1;
             else
                return 0;
     }                                                     36

